  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "وَ رَوَى عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ سِنَانٍ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ لَهُ:",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And ʿAbdullāh ibn Sinān narrated from Abī ʿAbdillāh عليه السلام, who said to him:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "quran_quote",
      "arabic_text": "«اِقْرَأْ «قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ» وَ «قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْكَافِرُونَ» عِنْدَ مَنَامِكَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "“Recite ‘Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad’ and ‘Qul yā ayyuhā al-kāfirūn’ at the time of your sleep”
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "فَإِنَّهَا بَرَاءَةٌ مِنَ الشِّرْكِ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "for they are a dissociation from shirk.”
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "quran_quote",
      "arabic_text": "وَ «قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ»",
      "translations": {
        "en": "And “‘Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad’”"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "closing",
      "arabic_text": "نِسْبَةُ الرَّبِّ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ.",
      "translations": {
        "en": "is the description of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith instructs reciting Sūrat al-Ikhlāṣ and Sūrat al-Kāfirūn before sleep. It presents these recitations as a declaration of disavowal from shirk and identifies Sūrat al-Ikhlāṣ as expressing the description of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic.",
      "seo_question": "What should be recited before sleep for freedom from shirk?",
      "key_terms": {
        "اِقْرَأْ": "Recite; an instruction to read these surahs before sleeping.",
        "مَنَامِكَ": "Your sleep; the time before going to sleep.",
        "بَرَاءَةٌ": "Dissociation or freedom; here, freedom from shirk.",
        "الشِّرْكِ": "Associating partners with Allah; the belief from which one disavows oneself.",
        "نِسْبَةُ": "Description or attribution; here, a defining description of the Lord.",
        "الرَّبِّ": "The Lord; Allah as the sustaining Lord.",
        "عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ": "Mighty and Majestic; an honorific expression for Allah."
      }
    }
  },
